        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Berlin</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1237 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">German merchants founded the twin settlements of Berlin and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colln">Cölln</a> at the end of the 12th century; it is unclear which is older, and 1237, the year of the first recorded mention of Cölln, was later taken as the founding date of the city.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the banks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spree">Spree</a> river in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, in low-lying marshy woodland on the Northern European Plain, surrounded by the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The twin towns of Berlin and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colln">Cölln</a>; the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> from 1701 and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> from 1871; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment">Enlightenment</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick the Great</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huguenots">Huguenots</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-potsdam">Edict of Potsdam</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar-republic">Weimar Republic</a> of the 1920s; the Nazi capital; the Berlin Blockade and airlift; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-wall">Berlin Wall</a> of 1961 to 1989</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Berlin is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and is also one of its states, with about 3.7 million inhabitants.</span></div>
